&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://coder.com&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Coder&lt;/a&gt; is a self-hosted platform for cloud development environments and AI coding agents. Workspaces are defined with Terraform, connected through a secure Wireguard® tunnel, and automatically shut down when not used. Coder Agents runs a native AI coding agent whose loop executes in the control plane on your infrastructure, with no API keys in workspaces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define cloud development environments in Terraform
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EC2 VMs, Kubernetes Pods, Docker Containers, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automatically shutdown idle resources to save on costs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Onboard developers in seconds instead of days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delegate coding work to AI agents on your infrastructure
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring any model (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, Bedrock, self-hosted)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No LLM credentials in workspaces, user identity on every action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Centralized model governance, cost tracking, and audit logging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;
  &lt;img src=&#34;./docs/images/hero-image.png&#34; alt=&#34;Coder platform showing templates and a running workspace&#34;&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;quickstart&#34;&gt;Quickstart
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check out our &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://coder.com/docs/install&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;install guides&lt;/a&gt; for other methods and a complete tutorial.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Try Coder with the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/coder/coder/blob/main/install.sh&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;install script&lt;/a&gt; on Linux and macOS, or grab the latest binary or installer from &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/coder/coder/releases/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;GitHub Releases&lt;/a&gt; on Windows:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-shell&#34; data-lang=&#34;shell&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;curl -L https://coder.com/install.sh &lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; sh
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Start the server and open &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;http://localhost:3000&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;http://localhost:3000&lt;/a&gt; to create your initial user, create a Docker template, and provision your first workspace:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-shell&#34; data-lang=&#34;shell&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;coder server
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;For a production deployment, add a PostgreSQL database (version 13 or later) and an external access URL, and see our &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://coder.com/docs/admin/infrastructure/validated-architectures&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;validated architectures&lt;/a&gt; for sizing and infrastructure guidance:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-shell&#34; data-lang=&#34;shell&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;coder server --postgres-url &amp;lt;url&amp;gt; --access-url &amp;lt;url&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Without these flags, Coder uses a built-in database and sets up a &lt;code&gt;*.try.coder.app&lt;/code&gt; access URL for evaluation. Use &lt;code&gt;coder --help&lt;/code&gt; for the full list of flags and environment variables.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;documentation&#34;&gt;Documentation
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Browse the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://coder.com/docs&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;documentation&lt;/a&gt; or visit a specific section below:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://coder.com/docs/user-guides/workspace-management&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workspaces&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Workspaces contain the IDEs, dependencies, and configuration information needed for software development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://coder.com/docs/admin/templates&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Templates&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Templates are written in Terraform and describe the infrastructure for workspaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://coder.com/docs/ai-coder/agents&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coder Agents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Delegate coding work to AI agents running on your self-hosted infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://coder.com/docs/ai-coder/ai-gateway&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Gateway&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Centralize authentication, auditing, and cost controls for AI tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://coder.com/docs/admin&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Administration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Learn how to operate Coder&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://coder.com/pricing#compare-plans&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Premium&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Learn about paid features built for large teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://coder.com/docs/user-guides/workspace-access&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;IDEs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Connect your existing editor to a workspace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;support&#34;&gt;Support
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/coder/coder/issues/new&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Open an issue&lt;/a&gt; for bugs and feature requests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For community support, showcasing what you built, and feedback on in-progress features, join our &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://discord.gg/coder&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Discord&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/coder/coder/discussions&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;GitHub Discussions&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dedicated support is included in Coder Premium. For more information, visit &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://coder.com/pricing&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;coder.com/pricing&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;integrations&#34;&gt;Integrations
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;New integrations are always in progress. Open an issue to request one. Contributions are welcome in any official or community repository.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;official&#34;&gt;Official
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://registry.coder.com&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coder Registry&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Templates, modules, and integrations for common development environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://registry.coder.com/modules?search=tag%3Aagent&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coding Agents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Run agents like Claude Code, Codex, and OpenCode isolated in Coder workspaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/coder/terraform-provider-coderd&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;coderd Terraform Provider&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Declaratively manage your Coder deployment configuration as code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=coder.coder-remote&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;VS Code Extension&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Open any Coder workspace in VS Code with a single click&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://plugins.jetbrains.com/plugin/26968-coder&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;JetBrains Toolbox Plugin&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Open any Coder workspace from JetBrains Toolbox with a single click&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://coder.com/docs/user-guides/devcontainers&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dev Containers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Build development environments using &lt;code&gt;devcontainer.json&lt;/code&gt; on Docker, Kubernetes, and OpenShift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/coder/coder-logstream-kube&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes Log Stream&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Stream Kubernetes Pod events to the Coder startup logs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/coder/code-marketplace&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Self-Hosted VS Code Extension Marketplace&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: A private extension marketplace that works in restricted or airgapped networks integrating with &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/coder/code-server&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;code-server&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/marketplace/actions/setup-coder&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;GitHub Actions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: An action to set up the Coder CLI in GitHub workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;community&#34;&gt;Community
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://cdr.co/discord-5hw2sjadGU&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coder Discord&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Chat with the community, get support, and hear about new product updates first&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://registry.coder.com/templates?search=status%3Acommunity&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Community Templates&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Community-contributed workspace templates in the Coder Registry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://registry.coder.com/modules?search=status%3Acommunity&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Community Modules&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: Community-contributed modules to extend Coder templates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/marketplace/actions/update-coder-template&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coder Template GitHub Action&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: A GitHub Action that updates Coder templates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/coder/agents-chat-action&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coder Agents Chat Action&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: A GitHub Action that starts a Coder Agents chat against a GitHub issue or pull request&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;contributing&#34;&gt;Contributing
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;New contributors are always welcome. If you are new to the Coder codebase, see
&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://coder.com/docs/about/contributing/CONTRIBUTING&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;the contribution guide&lt;/a&gt; to get started.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;hiring&#34;&gt;Hiring
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Apply on the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/coder?utm_source=github&amp;amp;utm_medium=readme&amp;amp;utm_campaign=unknown&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;careers page&lt;/a&gt; if you are interested in joining the team.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
